# Naming Conventions (your-project pack template)

Universal naming rules for this project. Layer-specific extras (Angular `sp-`
prefixes, NgRx action names, etc.) belong in the corresponding standards
skill, not here.

## Files

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| TS / JS source | kebab-case | `user-service.ts`, `auth-guard.ts` |
| React component | PascalCase OR kebab-case (pick one, stay consistent) | `UserCard.tsx` or `user-card.tsx` |
| Vue SFC | PascalCase or kebab-case (project-wide consistency) | `UserCard.vue` or `user-card.vue` |
| Test file | mirror source + `.spec` / `.test` | `user-service.spec.ts`, `UserResource.test.java` |
| Java class | PascalCase | `UserService.java`, `UserResource.java` |
| Java package | all lowercase, dot-separated | `com.example.users.service` |

## Identifiers

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Variables, fields | `camelCase` | `userId`, `lastLoginAt` |
| Functions, methods | `camelCase` (verb phrase) | `fetchUser`, `saveProfile` |
| Classes, interfaces, types | `PascalCase` | `UserService`, `PaymentResult` |
| Constants (module-level) | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_RETRIES`, `API_BASE_URL` |
| Enum values (TS / Java) | `PascalCase` (TS) or `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` (Java) | `Status.Active` (TS), `Status.ACTIVE` (Java) |
| Boolean accessors | `is*` / `has*` / `can*` prefix | `isActive`, `hasPermission`, `canEdit` |
| Private fields | language-idiomatic (no `_` prefix in TS class fields — use `#` private) | `#cache` (TS), `private cache` (Java) |

## Don't

- Don't abbreviate where the abbreviation isn't industry-standard. `userRepository` over `userRepo` in public APIs (internal short names are fine).
- Don't use single-letter variables outside of trivial loops (`i`, `j`) and well-known math conventions.
- Don't use language reserved words even where syntactically allowed (`type`, `interface`, `class` as variable names).
- Don't mix conventions within a file (e.g., some kebab-case files and some camelCase in the same folder).

## Layer-specific overrides

If a layer has its own conventions on top of these (Angular's `sp-` selector
prefix, NgRx `[Feature] Verb Description` action names, etc.), they live
in the corresponding standards skill — `your-project-angular18-standards.md`,
`your-project-react-standards.md`, etc.
